{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence","id":1213515,"title":"Transmuting an attack into Quintessence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-30T13:12:57-07:00","id":1213515,"title":"Transmuting an attack into Quintessence","content":"So with Forces 2 you can try and dampen an incoming attack. Change the path of a bullet, disperse a fiery strike, redirect a lightning bolt. It has to go somewhere, so the bullet ricochets or hits something else, the fire's embers lash out into the surroundings, and the lightning strikes something metallic around you.<br /> <br /> With Forces 3 you can transmute the incoming force. The bullet's velocity becomes heat, the fire becomes wind, the lightning becomes radiowaves, you get the picture.<br /> <br /> Now here's the bit that I find really surprising.<br /> <br /> Add Prime 4 to that transmutation effect, and you can transform the fire or lightning into pure Quintessence and absorb it. 1 point for every point of damage that you are converting.<br /> <br /> Say our attacking Mage is Arete 3, attacks with Forces 2, redirecting electricity from the mains, using their body as a conduit. Vulgar, but no witnesses, so it's difficulty 6. 2 successes, so that's 3 points of damage.<br /> <br /> The defending Mage has Arete 4, and is performing a vulgar Prime 4 Forces 3 feat, so that's difficulty 8. Their magical staff negates the raised difficulty from Rapid Casting. They spend a point of Willpower, since that's very sensible, and they also spend a point of Quintessence to push down the difficulty. 3 successes (2 of their 4 dice work out, plus the Willpower). They now absorb 3 points of Quintessence for a 2 Quintessence profit, and completely negate their foe's attack.<br /> <br /> That example isn't that crazy, since the defending Mage is more powerful. Here's my problem.<br /> <br /> A Mage could simply absorb Quintessence from a bonfire, using Forces 3 and Prime 4. Take half of the damage it's producing each turn as Quintessence and you'll be loaded up to your limit in no time.<br /> <br /> With that quirk of the rules, doesn't that make Nodes much less valuable for many Mages? Obviously not every Mage will accept gathering Quintessence from a bonfire as part of their paradigm, but many will. Whether the Dreamspeaker performs a ritual sacrifice to spiritual entities and dances around, absorbing the essence of fire spirits, or a Verbena leaps through the flames, using their sacred connection to the earth to emerge unburnt, or a Hermetic draws runes around a bonfire to invoke essential energies and draw out some primal force... you get the picture.<br /> <br /> Let's be conservative, very conservative, and say that a large bonfire could get you 5 Quintessence. We know a bonfire will have the potential to do more damage than that, but 5 will do. Throw a deer (large animal) on there to make it 15. Now you're a hippy burning a deer in the countryside, claiming to anyone who asks that it &quot;rejuvenates you&quot;. Heck, that might even be Coincidental; when I see hippies dancing around Stonehenge and coming out buzzing I assume they're high on drugs, not the primal essence of creation.<br /> <br /> With decent Stamina, the ritual will easily capture all of the Quintessence. And if it doesn't... well that's fine? Even if you only pick up 7 points, you've burnt a deer (easily caught with Spheres reducing difficulties for traps and hunting) and some wood (there's plenty of it).<br /> <br /> Why are nodes a big deal if this is possible? A level 5 node is a precious thing, but it's giving 10 Quintessence a week, -1 difficulty to magick, and a weaker Gauntlet. This is great, sure, but it doesn't seem that special when placed in perspective. And a weak Gauntlet and a Level 3 Cairn come with their own problems, of course, since Spirits aren't always friendly and Garou sure as hell aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-30-2018, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T15:03:10-07:00","id":1213541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence#post1213515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say our attacking Mage is Arete 3, attacks with Forces 2, redirecting electricity from the mains, using their body as a conduit. Vulgar, but no witnesses, so it's difficulty 6. 2 successes, so that's 3 points of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, scarily enough that's 6 levels of damage, FYI <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Forces adds one automatic success when it comes to the damage calculations, i.e. moves one slot further down on the damage table than what's rolled. Scary stuff.<br /> <br /> And your example about absorbing an attack and turning it into quintessence is technically right, however...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Mage could simply absorb Quintessence from a bonfire, using Forces 3 and Prime 4. Take half of the damage it's producing each turn as Quintessence and you'll be loaded up to your limit in no time. </div> </div> </div>..I think the bonfire would pretty much be extinguished after the first one, two absorptions. Remember that it would directly drain from the pattern itself, potentially snuffing the fire itself out of existance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With that quirk of the rules, doesn't that make Nodes much less valuable for many Mages? </div> </div> </div>Mages that have Prime 4 or higher in general tend not to have big problems with Quintessence anymore. They can completely deconstruct solid objects into pure Quintessence - it needn't even be an attack or something the like, and depending on their paradigm, they can absorb Quintessence purely from being at events that fit their belief. A Rave for a music-affine Ecstatic with Prime 4+ is the best thing ever.<br /> And Prime 5 Mages, of course, can sap Quintessence out of the free flow of quintessence anywhere, everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be conservative, very conservative, and say that a large bonfire could get you 5 Quintessence. We know a bonfire will have the potential to do more damage than that, but 5 will do. </div> </div> </div>I would not directly relate Quintessence to damage in every single case. For magickal attacks, maybe. For mundane fires and the like..I am not so sure. As an ST, I would certainly tone things down in case of non-Magickal patterns. But the point still stands: A Prime 4+ savvy Mage does not tend to have big Quintessence Problems. You are right about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why are nodes a big deal if this is possible? A level 5 node is a precious thing, but it's giving 10 Quintessence a week, -1 difficulty to magick, and a weaker Gauntlet. This is great, sure, but it doesn't seem that special when placed in perspective. And a weak Gauntlet and a Level 3 Cairn come with their own problems, of course, since Spirits aren't always friendly and Garou sure as hell aren't. </div> </div> </div>Exactly because almost every Mage can get Quintessence out of a Node, as well as Tass.<br /> Prime 4 isn't a thing you just learn over the course of a few months, or depending on character even a few years. Nor would every paradigm be fit for what you're suggesting.<br /> Nodes though? Nodes are universal, they can be used without causing paradox, pretty much every Paradigm probably acknowledges them because metaphysically they exist outside of paradigm. Even young mages can find a source of Quintessence in Nodes. The harvesting of Quintessence can probably even be automated under some technological paradigms, *and* they can be used to constantly fuel certain magickal constructs like Horizon Realms. Especially that last part makes them very important in the Ascension War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-30-2018, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T15:58:06-07:00","id":1213555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1213541#post1213541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, scarily enough that's 6 levels of damage, FYI <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Forces adds one automatic success when it comes to the damage calculations, i.e. moves one slot further down on the damage table than what's rolled. Scary stuff.<br /> <br /> And your example about absorbing an attack and turning it into quintessence is technically right, however...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ..I think the bonfire would pretty much be extinguished after the first one, two absorptions. Remember that it would directly drain from the pattern itself, potentially snuffing the fire itself out of existance.<br /> <br /> Mages that have Prime 4 or higher in general tend not to have big problems with Quintessence anymore. They can completely deconstruct solid objects into pure Quintessence - it needn't even be an attack or something the like, and depending on their paradigm, they can absorb Quintessence purely from being at events that fit their belief. A Rave for a music-affine Ecstatic with Prime 4+ is the best thing ever.<br /> And Prime 5 Mages, of course, caa sap Quintessence out of the free flow of quintessence anywhere, everywhere.<br /> <br /> I would not directly relate Quintessence to damage in every single case. For magickal attacks, maybe. For mundane fires and the like..I am not so sure. As an ST, I would certainly tone things down in case of non-Magickal patterns. But the point still stands: A Prime 4+ savvy Mage does not tend to have big Quintessence Problems. You are right about that.<br /> <br /> Exactly because almost every Mage can get Quintessence out of a Node, as well as Tass.<br /> Prime 4 isn't a thing you just learn over the course of a few months, or depending on character even a few years. Nor would every paradigm be fit for what you're suggesting.<br /> Nodes though? Nodes are universal, they can be used without causing paradox, pretty much every Paradigm probably acknowledges them because metaphysically they exist outside of paradigm. Even young mages can find a source of Quintessence in Nodes. The harvesting of Quintessence can probably even be automated under some technological paradigms, *and* they can be used to constantly fuel certain magickal constructs like Horizon Realms. Especially that last part makes them very important in the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> Hmm that all makes sense. I guess that Prime 4 having near-infinite access to Quintessence is just something I hadn't given much thought to. It's a feature not a bug, I guess.<br /> <br /> As for Forces Damage, I thought it added 1, rather than pushing it down 1 slot! That's terrifying. On an entirely unrelated note Forces 2 will be one of my first upgrade choices... cybernetic Lethal mega-damage punches here we come...<br /> <br /> And that makes sense. You don't even need Prime 1 for the node, just Avatar and some means of meditation. And with Prime 1 you can get a lot out of a node, so it's a great way for Mages to charge up without mastering Prime. With that said, I do feel like Prime is... almost the core Sphere? It's the source of everything, the power of creation, the power that fuels all Magick, countermagick, relates to the very core of patterns, establishes permanence, and destroys Paradox. And unlike some spheres it is amazing on its own, and with other spheres, in chronicles where the ST understands it really well (complicated resonance stuff, lots of niche ways of gathering Quintessence), and in chronicles where the ST's understanding is limited (simple node rules, creating stuff). So I don't really understand why a Mage wouldn't learn at least Prime 1 or 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:18:04-07:00","id":1213566,"title":"","content":"Because it eats up room for other spheres. Prime has its advantages sure, but not everyone is interested in becoming a living battery. Some people prefer to invest in Time for the promise the high level side of it can bring. Some people think matter and Entropy offer too many solutions. Some think that spirit is like having access to every other sphere provided you\u2019re gift of gab is on point enough, and some would say that correspondence is the real MVP (MVS?) giving you range and super surveillance. People might say that Forces is the only real Fight sphere of the lot, and Mind the best buff sphere, but Life 2\u2019s healing is far too important to not take.<br /> <br /> Also, how often do you use Quintessence, really? Some people always use it, others prefer to drop the difficulty of magic in other ways, with preparation, good skill rolls, making rotes, resonance, or just simply being coincidental with it all.<br /> Most magic that requires a large amount of quintessence to work tends to be Prime magic anyway, so for most mages, access to a node and an avatar of 3 is enough.<br /> <br /> I often tell my players that, eventually, every sphere at every level will become useful even Time 1, such as when one of my players woke up in a strange room and wondered how long they had been out. Or when another player found themselves in a 1920\u2019s New England bar, and couldn\u2019t tell what the heck was going on. Often times, the one sphere you absolutely need for a situation will always be the one you don\u2019t have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 04-30-2018, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T19:23:42-07:00","id":1213636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence#post1213515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are nodes a big deal if this is possible? A level 5 node is a precious thing, but it's giving 10 Quintessence a week, -1 difficulty to magick, and a weaker Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that how much Quintessence each dot of Node gives per week is dependent on Storyteller fiat. This description presupposes that the Storyteller is giving out the minimum amount. One point in Tass, and one point in &quot;free&quot; Quintessence. Implying a low(er)-magic setting, where every Quintessence point is precious, and things like Horizon Realms, Familiars, and Wonders (all of which require Quintessence) are few and far between. But the books themselves tell us that Storytellers are free to give out 5 or even 10 per dot per week, for a high(er)-magic campaign. Meaning that same level 5 Node can be giving out anywhere from 25 to 50(!) points a week.<br /> <br /> In light of that, the amount given by siphoning Quintessence from fires or material objects can almost seem like chump change. A solid option if you don't have a Node of your own, but hardly the Life Hack it's implied to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T22:19:43-07:00","id":1213675,"title":"","content":"This isn't cannon, it's just how I generally approached it. Nodes have resonance themselves, and the quintessence they create is coloured accordingly, but their resonance is a broad concept such as <i>creative urge </i>or <i>enlightenment</i>. You can frame a lot of effects through that. You can rule that drawing quintessence from objects has the quintessence become very heavily coloured by the resonance of the item. So the juice gained from a bonfire can create, well, fire. That's it. Keeping it in your pattern for long amounts of time might colour it with your own soul's resonance, in which case you're golden, but you can contain only so much, and you need to wait for the process to happen. Drawing quintessence from living things is better, since the living have more expansive concepts to their resonance, but you need to get through the antithetical resonance issue - ie, get a willing sacrifice. <br /> <br /> Exceptions include treasured keepsakes, which bear the resonance of the owner, and unique items that have symbolic value to a lot of people, which bear the appropriate resonance (a pebble from the Parthenon). <br /> <br /> In the case of a Scientific Paradigm, ignore the above mumbo jumbo. It's just a matter of energy conversion. If you want to make a bonfire heat something, it's energy transference, but if you want to make a bonfire into a bowl of petunias, then you need to make so many energy conversions that the productivity of your effect is crap.<br /> <br /> Taking all this into consideration, quintessence is a limited resource in the short term. Prime 4 mages still have a serious benefit - they can probably start a story with 20 points, as they can reasonably claim to have absorbed enough object quintessence for long enough for it to become keyed to them. And they can still use quintessence from objects, just in a far more limited fashion.<br /> <br /> <u>Note</u><b>: </b>If you're playing with the 10 quintessence per dot per week, ignore this. You effectively are giving infinite quintessence, unless you make nodes insanely rare.<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>TL;DR</b></u></i>: You can rule that quintessence is heavily afflicted with resonance from its (object) source, to the point that it can only effectively replicate its source until it is cleaned through time spent in the mage's pattern - thus making untainted quintessence fitting for any effect rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T03:41:05-07:00","id":1213723,"title":"","content":"resonance of tass can be refined. Think about petrol and uranium. I'm not sure what prime level is required to build a refinery. I'd say 2-5 depending on the paradigm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:34:59-07:00","id":1213739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1213566#post1213566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it eats up room for other spheres. Prime has its advantages sure, but not everyone is interested in becoming a living battery. Some people prefer to invest in Time for the promise the high level side of it can bring. Some people think matter and Entropy offer too many solutions. Some think that spirit is like having access to every other sphere provided you\u2019re gift of gab is on point enough, and some would say that correspondence is the real MVP (MVS?) giving you range and super surveillance. People might say that Forces is the only real Fight sphere of the lot, and Mind the best buff sphere, but Life 2\u2019s healing is far too important to not take.<br /> <br /> Also, how often do you use Quintessence, really? Some people always use it, others prefer to drop the difficulty of magic in other ways, with preparation, good skill rolls, making rotes, resonance, or just simply being coincidental with it all.<br /> Most magic that requires a large amount of quintessence to work tends to be Prime magic anyway, so for most mages, access to a node and an avatar of 3 is enough.<br /> <br /> I often tell my players that, eventually, every sphere at every level will become useful even Time 1, such as when one of my players woke up in a strange room and wondered how long they had been out. Or when another player found themselves in a 1920\u2019s New England bar, and couldn\u2019t tell what the heck was going on. Often times, the one sphere you absolutely need for a situation will always be the one you don\u2019t have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! That's a great perspective.<br /> <br /> I feel like since Prime 1 shows the flow of magical energy, allowing you to recognise Mages and Nightfolk, I would argue that Prime 1 will usually be a sensible investment, unless a concept REALLY needs 3 dots in 2 specific Spheres. And without Prime 1 you will never have more Quintessence than your Avatar rating; you could be sitting in a Level 10 Node and you'd still be stuck at 0-5 points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T06:11:03-07:00","id":1213769,"title":"","content":"Depends on how much of a presence other nightfolk have in your games. Besides, Spirit can be used to recognise the garou and wraiths, and Life with Matter can be used to detect vampires.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the most sought after first level sphere has been Mind, the buffs and free WP rolls to save against being mind controlled is usually enough for people, while corr 1 remains a really popular alternative. Prime 1\u2019s extra Quintessence capacity starts to become much less useful once paradox begins to pile on.<br /> <br /> I house rule it so that if you don\u2019t have Prime1, you can still have more Quintessence than your avatar, but it slowly bleeds off you at a rate of 1 point per day down to your Avatar rating. And this excess Quintessence can be easily taken by other Prime mages, and makes you shine like a torch in Prime vision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 05-01-2018, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T16:56:20-07:00","id":1213969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1213769#post1213769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how much of a presence other nightfolk have in your games. Besides, Spirit can be used to recognise the garou and wraiths, and Life with Matter can be used to detect vampires.<br /> <br /> In my experience, the most sought after first level sphere has been Mind, the buffs and free WP rolls to save against being mind controlled is usually enough for people, while corr 1 remains a really popular alternative. Prime 1\u2019s extra Quintessence capacity starts to become much less useful once paradox begins to pile on.<br /> <br /> I house rule it so that if you don\u2019t have Prime1, you can still have more Quintessence than your avatar, but it slowly bleeds off you at a rate of 1 point per day down to your Avatar rating. And this excess Quintessence can be easily taken by other Prime mages, and makes you shine like a torch in Prime vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well even just seeing that a person is using Magick is a big deal, and Prime 1 can let you see effects on a metaphysical level.<br /> <br /> Mind 1 and Correspondence 1 are pretty awesome too. Personally I think that Mage gives a lot of great non-Sphere options in character gen, like Augmentations, Do, Wonders and Devices, so starting with 1 in 6 Spheres could be a good option. You just need to make the most of the sensory advantage, and the difficulty reductions that come with it. Make a mega martial artist whose hits always land perfectly (difficulty 2 from Well Trained Advantage and Arete successes), and then when you learn Forces 2 things get pushed up a gear. And I feel like starting off with few options for direct manipulation will mean that you make more use of the Rank 2 spheres as you acquire them one by one. There's a mild EXP advantage to building wide (1x6 and 2x3 are the most efficient, 2's are awkward in terms of Freebies vs EXP) as well.<br /> <br /> The Quintessence is arguably more useful when you have lots of Paradox; reducing difficulties means fewer botches, and that means you won't get that fatal backlash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T00:17:43-07:00","id":1214065,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s great that you find prime so essential. I have only come across a handful of players who think so. <br /> <br /> Staving of paradox is a double edged sword. It can be better to have many small backlashes than one big one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T00:30:10-07:00","id":1214069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214065#post1214065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s great that you find prime so essential. I have only come across a handful of players who think so.<br /> <br /> Staving of paradox is a double edged sword. It can be better to have many small backlashes than one big one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, but I was under the impression that Soulgems could take up Paradox? There are ways of managing it below level 5. And Prime makes managing a Familiar achievable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T00:51:13-07:00","id":1214076,"title":"","content":"Personally, my #1 killer app for Prime remains the relatively low-level application of creation Ex Nihilo. Prime 2 + &lt;Pattern&gt;.<br /> <br /> It's useful and justifyable for a vast array of paradigms in one form or another, it's relatively low level, has lots of uses from basic 'Cast fireball' to downright bizarre creations, does ICly take a <i>relatively</i> short time to learn, and especially with Forces just constitutes a very basic staple for many magic tropes.<br /> <br /> It's kind of an essential component for a vast category of effects, just like Correspondence 2 is the big <i>'Do lots of different neat little things over a distance'</i> enabler. If I have a character on the menu that has Prime in their reportoire, it's usually to that level, unless the character is more specialized. Wonder crafter, Chorister, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T14:10:50-07:00","id":1214312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214076#post1214076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, my #1 killer app for Prime remains the relatively low-level application of creation Ex Nihilo. Prime 2 + &lt;Pattern&gt;.<br /> <br /> It's useful and justifyable for a vast array of paradigms in one form or another, it's relatively low level, has lots of uses from basic 'Cast fireball' to downright bizarre creations, does ICly take a <i>relatively</i> short time to learn, and especially with Forces just constitutes a very basic staple for many magic tropes.<br /> <br /> It's kind of an essential component for a vast category of effects, just like Correspondence 2 is the big <i>'Do lots of different neat little things over a distance'</i> enabler. If I have a character on the menu that has Prime in their reportoire, it's usually to that level, unless the character is more specialized. Wonder crafter, Chorister, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 2 is also useful for creating Charms (if you've got the right Tass), and for enchanting weapons and clothes to inflict and soak Aggravated damage, respectively. It's far more coincidental to cut a guy with a Prime-enchanted sword than to summon one from raw Quintessence. Cheaper too, if you go by HDYDT? rules. And you need one less dot in Prime to make regular weapons enchanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T01:23:20-07:00","id":1214473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214076#post1214076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, my #1 killer app for Prime remains the relatively low-level application of creation Ex Nihilo. Prime 2 + &lt;Pattern&gt;.<br /> <br /> It's useful and justifyable for a vast array of paradigms in one form or another, it's relatively low level, has lots of uses from basic 'Cast fireball' to downright bizarre creations, does ICly take a <i>relatively</i> short time to learn, and especially with Forces just constitutes a very basic staple for many magic tropes.<br /> <br /> It's kind of an essential component for a vast category of effects, just like Correspondence 2 is the big <i>'Do lots of different neat little things over a distance'</i> enabler. If I have a character on the menu that has Prime in their reportoire, it's usually to that level, unless the character is more specialized. Wonder crafter, Chorister, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like a lot of the Spheres really shine at level 2. Correspondence 2, Prime 2, Forces 2 I believe you can just conjure up an orb of Quintessence and move it around like a pinball of death, from afar. Matter 2, Prime 2, you can toughen your clothing and protective gear to raise it's Armour rating, and then you can allow it to soak Aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T01:31:14-07:00","id":1214474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214312#post1214312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime 2 is also useful for creating Charms (if you've got the right Tass), and for enchanting weapons and clothes to inflict and soak Aggravated damage, respectively. It's far more coincidental to cut a guy with a Prime-enchanted sword than to summon one from raw Quintessence. Cheaper too, if you go by HDYDT? rules. And you need one less dot in Prime to make regular weapons enchanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely sure on Charms vs. Wonders. And yes, Prime 2 is really amazing.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that upgrading all of the Spheres you have to 2 might be a better investment than pushing one of them to 3 or higher. Would depend on the concept obviously. But with 2 in Life, Matter, Forces, Correspondence, Prime and Mind, you have a long list of powerful and Coincidental effects. Sure, direct mind control is more powerful than gentle nudges, but that's +1 difficulty for the higher level and +1/2 difficulty from being Vulgar (quite often). And yes controlling a whole forest fire is really awesome, but it's not nearly as useful as just turning one person into ash (most of the time).<br /> <br /> The main draw of level 4 Spheres, for me, are the Specs. Beyond that, Level 1 and 2 feel like they are (in a very general way) the safest and most subtle way of approaching problems. And when you run into something that is quite central to your character's advancement, which requires a higher level in a Spheres (making Wonders, healing others, handling large groups of foes) you can work towards that off of a strong base, if you know what I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T02:23:36-07:00","id":1214487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214473#post1214473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a lot of the Spheres really shine at level 2. Correspondence 2, Prime 2, Forces 2 I believe you can just conjure up an orb of Quintessence and move it around like a pinball of death, from afar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmnah.<br /> First off, it does not require Forces as Quintessence only requires Prime to control it...it is nothing physical. And you would require Prime 3 to conjure it freely like that..and thus also Correspondence 3.<br /> But yes, Correspondence 3, Prime 3 is..nasty.<br /> Especially if you go by pure actual lore of what Quintessence is, and what it does to patterns when used like that. There is *technically* no way to soak it except through Prime enhancement or other supernatural protection...although by the rules, of course, it is simply 'aggravated damage'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get the feeling that upgrading all of the Spheres you have to 2 might be a better investment than pushing one of them to 3 or higher. </div> </div> </div>Yes. In general, you have much more flexibility and possibilities when spreading your investment across more spheres, than when going for a few but high spheres <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The possible combinations of spheres and effects grow exponentially. You just won't have access to certain high level effecst as early as those more specialized in a few spheres from the get-go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T02:30:42-07:00","id":1214491,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> I'm adding Forces for two reasons.<br /> <br /> 1: I'm throwing an orb of death around, so Forces will, in a theoretical sense, give a refined aspect to the movement and attack.<br /> <br /> 2: This adds an extra rank of damage.<br /> <br /> It isn't necessary, but when it's the difference between 2 and 6 points of Aggravated damage it's certainly worth it.<br /> <br /> And I see... hmm. So actually conjuring up pure Quintessence is Rank 3... well at the very least you could pick up a blade (Correspondence 2, Forces 2) and then charge it with Quintessence (Prime 2) and slice up everyone in the room.<br /> <br /> Yeah that's the impression I got! I like the idea of flexibility and exponential growth. I could only imagine starting with 3 in a Sphere if it were critical to a backstory or their mechanical concept; a healer should start with the ability to heal others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-03-2018, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T02:53:26-07:00","id":1214501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214491#post1214491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> I'm adding Forces for two reasons.<br /> <br /> 1: I'm throwing an orb of death around, so Forces will, in a theoretical sense, give a refined aspect to the movement and attack.<br /> <br /> 2: This adds an extra rank of damage.<br /> <br /> It isn't necessary, but when it's the difference between 2 and 6 points of Aggravated damage it's certainly worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, here is the thing:<br /> <br /> * If said ball of death is actually made of Quintessence instead of a force, the Forces sphere won't do anything to it - not for steering the ball since that only can get done with Prime as forces do not influence Quintessence, nor for Damage as the ball itself is not made of something the Forces sphere governs. The damage increase only counts for attacking *with* a Force. Fire, Electicity, etc.<br /> Prime 3 and Correspondence 3 are enough in this case for the remote Quintessence ball of death.<br /> <br /> * If the ball is *made* of a Force, you need Forces 3 to conjure it to a remote location ( If the force is not present at the remote place ), and thus also need Correspondence 3 since Correspondence needs to be at the same level than the largest other sphere in the effect <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You only need Prime 2 for the creation ex nihilo though, yeah.<br /> <br /> So, either Prime 3, Correspondence 3 and a point of Quintessence, or Forces 3, Correspondence 3 Prime 2. No Quintessence point required in the latter case since it is not a permanent conjuration, you get more raw damage, but the damage is also potentially soakable in more ways depending on what the force is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-03-2018, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T03:02:02-07:00","id":1214503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214501#post1214501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, here is the thing:<br /> <br /> * If said ball of death is actually made of Quintessence instead of a force, the Forces sphere won't do anything to it - not for steering the ball since that only can get done with Prime as forces do not influence Quintessence, nor for Damage as the ball itself is not made of something the Forces sphere governs. The damage increase only counts for attacking *with* a Force. Fire, Electicity, etc.<br /> Prime 3 and Correspondence 3 are enough in this case for the remote Quintessence ball of death.<br /> <br /> * If the ball is *made* of a Force, you need Forces 3 to conjure it to a remote location ( If the force is not present at the remote place ), and thus also need Correspondence 3 since Correspondence needs to be at the same level than the largest other sphere in the effect <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You only need Prime 2 for the creation ex nihilo though, yeah.<br /> <br /> So, either Prime 3, Correspondence 3 and a point of Quintessence, or Forces 3, Correspondence 3 Prime 2. No Quintessence point required in the latter case since it is not a permanent conjuration, you get more raw damage, but the damage is also potentially soakable in more ways depending on what the force is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 3 is only needed for force-related transmutations, so I'm sure there's a way I can figure this...<br /> <br /> The goal is horrible Aggravated damage from range. If that's the goal, there will be a way to do it with only Level 2 Spheres.<br /> <br /> So you use Correspondence 2 to examine the site. Find a potential weapon. Charge it up with Prime, move it with Forces, murder everyone. Results may vary depending on who/what you're targeting ;-)<br /> <br /> As for the Quintessence cost; summoning up a ball of Quintessence will cost 1 Quintessence per turn. M20 has it so that if you make a blade or projectile using Prime, those are costly, 1 Quint per turn/blast. I was under the impression that creating something &quot;Ex Nihilo&quot; will always cost one point of Quintessence also. If you want to create a pattern like a Fire, then you'll need fuel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T04:46:13-07:00","id":1214531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214503#post1214503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was under the impression that creating something &quot;Ex Nihilo&quot; will always cost one point of Quintessence also. If you want to create a pattern like a Fire, then you'll need fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Phil clarified that - creating something out of nothing does not cost Quintessence per se - with exceptions.<br /> <br /> * Objects will vanish again after the spell duration has passed, unless you invest Quintessence into the creation. I think the HDYDT FAQ actually mentions this as well. This is especially worth keeping in mind when you want to create something like, say..food.<br /> * Forces can last for a turn - casting a fireball, a lightning bolt, etc. Only if the force is supposed to last longer than a round it needs either Quintessence or mundane sources to prolong its existance. But the initial round of creation is 'free'.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to cause aggravated damge from a distance with minimal investment of spheres, Forces 2 Correspondence 2 would be enough - if a source of a force is nearby.<br /> And in the modern world, it's hard not to find a spot where you can overload an electrical gadget, make a flame burst into a fire, or cause related malfunctions - especially if a powerline nearby is faulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T04:51:53-07:00","id":1214533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214531#post1214531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Phil clarified that - creating something out of nothing does not cost Quintessence per se - with exceptions.<br /> <br /> * Objects will vanish again after the spell duration has passed, unless you invest Quintessence into the creation. I think the HDYDT FAQ actually mentions this as well. This is especially worth keeping in mind when you want to create something like, say..food.<br /> * Forces can last for a turn - casting a fireball, a lightning bolt, etc. Only if the force is supposed to last longer than a round it needs either Quintessence or mundane sources to prolong its existance. But the initial round of creation is 'free'.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to cause aggravated damge from a distance with minimal investment of spheres, Forces 2 Correspondence 2 would be enough - if a source of a force is nearby.<br /> And in the modern world, it's hard not to find a spot where you can overload an electrical gadget, make a flame burst into a fire, or cause related malfunctions - especially if a powerline nearby is faulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh so if you make water out of nothing, it won't stick around unless you invest in the pattern and make it &quot;real&quot;. But if you drink water that is going to disappear, do you lose the water from your body as it fades?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T04:55:41-07:00","id":1214536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214533#post1214533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh so if you make water out of nothing, it won't stick around unless you invest in the pattern and make it &quot;real&quot;. But if you drink water that is going to disappear, do you lose the water from your body as it fades?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to that is &quot;Undefined&quot;. There are two ways one can argue:<br /> <br /> *Either the water inside the body vanishes at the time the spell ends<br /> * Or it does not vanish because it has become part of the life pattern.<br /> <br /> Of course an argument against the latter would be 'Well, if the life pattern is making the water 'real' through a natural infusion of the life pattern's quintessence, then the water would potentially make you more thirsty, not less&quot;.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: ST Fiat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T05:26:43-07:00","id":1214544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214531#post1214531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Phil clarified that - creating something out of nothing does not cost Quintessence per se - with exceptions.<br /> <br /> * Objects will vanish again after the spell duration has passed, unless you invest Quintessence into the creation. I think the HDYDT FAQ actually mentions this as well. This is especially worth keeping in mind when you want to create something like, say..food.<br /> * Forces can last for a turn - casting a fireball, a lightning bolt, etc. Only if the force is supposed to last longer than a round it needs either Quintessence or mundane sources to prolong its existance. But the initial round of creation is 'free'.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to cause aggravated damge from a distance with minimal investment of spheres, Forces 2 Correspondence 2 would be enough - if a source of a force is nearby.<br /> And in the modern world, it's hard not to find a spot where you can overload an electrical gadget, make a flame burst into a fire, or cause related malfunctions - especially if a powerline nearby is faulty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Before we knew this, we expected every kind of Forces 3 Prime 2 effect that for example conjures fire, would use a point of quintessence since you can't just conjure energy or mass out of pure nothingness, needing at least a bit of metaphysical energy and then the amount of successes you have determine your &quot;efficiency&quot; so to say.<br /> <br /> And we kept this for balancing purposes since, as already said, direct forces attacks are nasty. <br /> This also makes quintessence into a much more precious resource, increasing the need for nodes or other sources of quintessence and limiting the character's massive destructive abilities to one to five spells most of the times. (Also, you might need to heal aggravated damage, which of course also needs quintessence since it's pattern damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13530-queen-nihil","name":"Queen Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13530_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T05:37:18-07:00","id":1214548,"title":"","content":"Idea; turn cyanide into water, and have someone drink it. They could even find that it's water if they used Matter 1. And then after a while it turns back (no Quintessence invested, transmutation is temporary) and any of the water which hasn't been metabolised is now a lethal toxin. D e a d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T05:48:36-07:00","id":1214553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Nihil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214544#post1214544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before we knew this, we expected every kind of Forces 3 Prime 2 effect that for example conjures fire, would use a point of quintessence since you can't just conjure energy or mass out of pure nothingness, needing at least a bit of metaphysical energy and then the amount of successes you have determine your &quot;efficiency&quot; so to say.<br /> <br /> And we kept this for balancing purposes since, as already said, direct forces attacks are nasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if it really is a balancing solution - remember that Forces 3 lets you transmute one force into another. So to create a Fireball without using Quintessence with that ruling, instead of conjuring it out of nothing simply transmute all the heat, light, sound, what-have-you in the room into a fireball. or, you know, even just transmut some matter into fire, if you have the sphers.<br /> Wether to use that method or rely on conjuration becomes a matter of paradigm.<br /> <br /> I personally consider the requirement to use Quintessence to make conjured objects permanent a much bigger justifier for the necessity of a Node, in the grand scheme of things. Acquiring building materials, alchemical resources, weapons, food storages and what-have-you for Chantries, Sanctums, Horizon Realms, personal hideouts or just everyday niceties and/or 'Off the Grid' makes a source of Quintessence a necessity.<br /> Many things can be acquired though manual labor and/or according finances - but depending on what you have planned, they can also seriously cut into the time a Mage might otherwise have available.<br /> The #1 'Must have Quintessence!' reason for me still remains the lowering of effect difficulties, especially in a pinch. I always, *always* would want to have a pile of Quint available just for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-03-2018, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T05:54:56-07:00","id":1214555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214553#post1214553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many things can be acquired though manual labor and/or according finances - but depending on what you have planned, they can also seriously cut into the time a Mage might otherwise have available.<br /> The #1 'Must have Quintessence!' reason for me still remains the lowering of effect difficulties, especially in a pinch. I always, *always* would want to have a pile of Quint available just for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Any Mage, given time to make 2 or 3 rolls, can escape a life-or-death situation. But you don't always have time to roll a few times, and sometimes there is ZERO margin of error. Either you teleport away from the combat-blender-of-death, or you're mage soup. And in that situation, dropping the difficulty to 3 is a huge deal and could save your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:09:41-07:00","id":1214560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214548#post1214548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idea; turn cyanide into water, and have someone drink it. They could even find that it's water if they used Matter 1. And then after a while it turns back (no Quintessence invested, transmutation is temporary) and any of the water which hasn't been metabolised is now a lethal toxin. D e a d.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a Matter 2 rote, and would not require Quintessence, or even prime magic at all, to be made permanent. With Matter, the assumption is it\u2019s permanent unless you put a limit on it (i.e. put successes into duration).<br /> <br /> Also, Matter 1 would definitely pick up on the transformation if there was a limit placed on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:18:00-07:00","id":1214564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214555#post1214555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Any Mage, given time to make 2 or 3 rolls, can escape a life-or-death situation. But you don't always have time to roll a few times, and sometimes there is ZERO margin of error. Either you teleport away from the combat-blender-of-death, or you're mage soup. And in that situation, dropping the difficulty to 3 is a huge deal and could save your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there are concequences with having a huge pool of quintessence within you. For one thing you are incredibly visible from the spirit realm. For another you seem more noticeable, more real, attracting attention of passerby\u2019s and potentially working against arcane. If you want a low profile, carrying a tonne of quintessence is not the way to do it, especially in the spirit realm where all kinds of beings would see you as a potential snack.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good way to spike up on the technocracy\u2019s radar as well as attract the ire of the garou who would see you as having stolen from Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:22:12-07:00","id":1214565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214564#post1214564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But there are concequences with having a huge pool of quintessence within you. For one thing you are incredibly visible from the spirit realm. For another you seem more noticeable, more real, attracting attention of passerby\u2019s and potentially working against arcane. If you want a low profile, carrying a tonne of quintessence is not the way to do it, especially in the spirit realm where all kinds of beings would see you as a potential snack.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a good way to spike up on the technocracy\u2019s radar as well as attract the ire of the garou who would see you as having stolen from Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as long as you stay under 5 (or whatever your Avatar rating is) none of those should be a problem. The energy is seen, metaphysically speaking, as a normal part of your pattern. So you won't stand out any more than another Mage.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;running hot&quot;, I feel like if those problems became a recurring issue, then a Mage could devise a rote to hide the strength of their resonance and how much energy they are carrying, right? For example, a Prime / Mind rote could give the impression (Mind 2) or the illusion (Mind 4 I think?) that you are carrying a normal amount of energy. Think of it like &quot;Hiding your power level&quot; in DBZ, if that make sense.<br /> <br /> And Werewolves can just... &quot;stolen from Gaia&quot;. You'd think they would have better things to do than kill random Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:35:55-07:00","id":1214572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214565#post1214565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well as long as you stay under 5 (or whatever your Avatar rating is) none of those should be a problem. The energy is seen, metaphysically speaking, as a normal part of your pattern. So you won't stand out any more than another Mage.<br /> <br /> As for &amp;quot;running hot&amp;quot;, I feel like if those problems became a recurring issue, then a Mage could devise a rote to hide the strength of their resonance and how much energy they are carrying, right? For example, a Prime / Mind rote could give the impression (Mind 2) or the illusion (Mind 4 I think?) that you are carrying a normal amount of energy. Think of it like &amp;quot;Hiding your power level&amp;quot; in DBZ, if that make sense.<br /> <br /> And Werewolves can just... &amp;quot;stolen from Gaia&amp;quot;. You'd think they would have better things to do than kill random Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then having Prime 1 isn\u2019t all that necessary since you\u2019ll be below your avatar anyway.<br /> <br /> You could, but the more ongoing effects you have, the more detectable you are via prime, and the harder doing other magic becomes. Nothing is ever concequence free.<br /> <br /> Wereloves literally run on rage. What is rational doesn\u2019t always enter into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:41:01-07:00","id":1214575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214572#post1214572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then having Prime 1 isn\u2019t all that necessary since you\u2019ll be below your avatar anyway.<br /> <br /> You could, but the more ongoing effects you have, the more detectable you are via prime, and the harder doing other magic becomes. Nothing is ever concequence free.<br /> <br /> Wereloves literally run on rage. What is rational doesn\u2019t always enter into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm that's a good point. But even if you're staying below your Avatar rating, Prime helps you to find sources of Quintessence. And with a soulgem you could always &quot;stock&quot; your Quintessence in your sanctum (or chantry space) when you need to keep a low profile. If you needed the power in an emergency, a coincidental effect could have you pulling your soulgem out of your jacket pocket (Correspondence 3 I think?).<br /> <br /> Surely the penalties for ongoing effects only count if you're consciously maintaining them? So if you cast this &quot;yeah no energy, nothing to see here&quot; Prime/Mind effect, and get a certain duration (a day, a few hours) then surely you don't need to focus on maintaining it? What determines whether an effect needs to be consciously maintained, essentially?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:51:15-07:00","id":1214581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214575#post1214575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm that's a good point. But even if you're staying below your Avatar rating, Prime helps you to find sources of Quintessence. And with a soulgem you could always &quot;stock&quot; your Quintessence in your sanctum (or chantry space) when you need to keep a low profile. If you needed the power in an emergency, a coincidental effect could have you pulling your soulgem out of your jacket pocket (Correspondence 3 I think?).<br /> <br /> Surely the penalties for ongoing effects only count if you're consciously maintaining them? So if you cast this &quot;yeah no energy, nothing to see here&quot; Prime/Mind effect, and get a certain duration (a day, a few hours) then surely you don't need to focus on maintaining it? What determines whether an effect needs to be consciously maintained, essentially?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could carry around a perriapt. You don\u2019t need Prime to fill them, draw from them, or strictly speaking make them. Just have a few in your node absorbing the quintessence, and keep them close when it\u2019s time to party.<br /> <br /> An effect is ongoing if it is not instantaneous or permanent. This applies to literally all effects. The only way to make an effect permanent is with a boatload of successes an quintesssnce, and therefore would arguably require prime just to mamas the quintessence necessary for larger effects. Absolutely requires prime in the case of wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T07:25:24-07:00","id":1214591,"title":"","content":"Prime it's extremely usefull, however I can imagine mages without it.<br /> <br /> For instance, Entropy it's also a beast of a Sphere and, since it's potential relies on out-lucking the opposition, it doesn't relly so much on things like creating stuff and the difficulty it's already low (a decent Avatar/Periapt, a Node and a specialized Instrument should cover your needs there). With Entropy 3 / Corr 3 your enemies would be running from cars and evading falling bricks and flower vases all day long while you rest in your Node (which already lowers your diff and get's you Quintessence for that time when you go outside or to stave off Domino Effect). You just need to outsource a Prime user for when you want a Wonder.<br /> <br /> Still Prime 1 it's undoubtedly useful. Detect supernatural influences in a mage story it's often useful and you can always have extra Quint unless your wheel it's chocked on Paradox (even with Avatar 5, you would need 15 points of 'dox to get to the point where Prime 1 can't give you anything - that's a lot of 'dox). And the Sphere only gets better from that point onwards - definitely a worthy investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-03-2018, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T07:34:00-07:00","id":1214593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214591#post1214591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime it's extremely usefull, however I can imagine mages without it.<br /> <br /> For instance, Entropy it's also a beast of a Sphere and, since it's potential relies on out-lucking the opposition, it doesn't relly so much on things like creating stuff and the difficulty it's already low (a decent Avatar/Periapt, a Node and a specialized Instrument should cover your needs there). With Entropy 3 / Corr 3 your enemies would be running from cars and evading falling bricks and flower vases all day long while you rest in your Node (which already lowers your diff and get's you Quintessence for that time when you go outside or to stave off Domino Effect). You just need to outsource a Prime user for when you want a Wonder.<br /> <br /> Still Prime 1 it's undoubtedly useful. Detect supernatural influences in a mage story it's often useful and you can always have extra Quint unless your wheel it's chocked on Paradox (even with Avatar 5, you would need 15 points of 'dox to get to the point where Prime 1 can't give you anything - that's a lot of 'dox). And the Sphere only gets better from that point onwards - definitely a worthy investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... the annoying thing is that I want ALL of them. I mean I can live without Time, and Spirit is only worthwhile (IMO) if you base the concept around it and invest in the idea of a spiritually aligned Mage. Otherwise the Spirit side of things is a distracting dimension (figuratively and literally).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T10:16:32-07:00","id":1214662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214593#post1214593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... the annoying thing is that I want ALL of them. I mean I can live without Time, and Spirit is only worthwhile (IMO) if you base the concept around it and invest in the idea of a spiritually aligned Mage. Otherwise the Spirit side of things is a distracting dimension (figuratively and literally).</div> </div> </div> </div>This literally sounds like a young Mage - probably of the Traditions - who is still somehow stuck in a down-to-earth way of thinking. One thing is not learning the Sphere of Spirit - this can be a personal choice, or due to circumstances, or because of both of those reasons. But mocking this part of Magick like this ? I think this would be censured in the Traditions.<br /> <br /> If you need a purely practical reason, then the opportunities to travel using the Umbra and to hide in the Umbra should be reasons enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-03-2018, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T11:46:32-07:00","id":1214700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214662#post1214662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This literally sounds like a young Mage - probably of the Traditions - who is still somehow stuck in a down-to-earth way of thinking. One thing is not learning the Sphere of Spirit - this can be a personal choice, or due to circumstances, or because of both of those reasons. But mocking this part of Magick like this ? I think this would be censured in the Traditions.<br /> <br /> If you need a purely practical reason, then the opportunities to travel using the Umbra and to hide in the Umbra should be reasons enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I think that Spirit is amazing. It's one of my favourite Spheres. But I feel like it's quite specialized. If I wanted to play a Mage with Spirit, I would focus very much on the spiritual side of it, in their backstory, their Abilities, their Backgrounds, their personality, their views on the world. A technomage with an alien companion, a shaman (perhaps Kinfolk) with a strong tie to the umbra, a dreaming mage with an extensive demesne and fae blood, a Hermetic who messes around with potent Spirits, warding, binding, bargaining.<br /> <br /> I mean Spirit has some simple applications which are always useful. Awakening the spirits of objects, stepping sideways, defending yourself from Spirits... but a lot of its most powerful applications require a lot of investment, and I don't just mean the dots in Spirit. In order to make the most of the Sphere you need to have a lot besides the Sphere itself.<br /> <br /> So the main thing is that I simply wouldn't want Spirit on my sheet unless I was devoting a lot of energy to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T13:56:05-07:00","id":1214756,"title":"","content":"Well thats true for all spheres. A sphere itself is not sufficient, you have to possess the skills that go with it if you want to play it right. You can always play it &quot;easy mode&quot;.<br /> For example,imagine a VA who sees programs as spirits, who can be coerced by knowing their vulnerabilities.<br /> Put all the dots in Spirit, Manipulation, and Computer (Minimum 4, specialization Cybersecurity), and Voil\u00e0.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T14:11:30-07:00","id":1214766,"title":"","content":"One of my characters, an Etherite got Spirit 1 simply because they got fed up of all this spirit stuff happening around them and not having any way of understanding what was going on. They read a few books during downtime and started to study ways to measure spiritual energy, and from then on, they could at least keep up with everyone else once spirit stuff started to go down. It wasn\u2019t really their focus or interest, but it helped, at least for targeting spirits with magic stuff. (My ST probably should have left it to spirit 2 strictly speaking, but they allowed it)<br /> <br /> This mage had no interest in spirits otherwise, nor any real wish to ever traverse the umbra, not after the first time the crosses the gauntlet and their avatar was shredded, but with all the otherworldly stuff that was jumping out at them throughout the story, knowing at least a little Spirit was just becoming a necessity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T14:50:32-07:00","id":1214781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214766#post1214766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my characters, an Etherite got Spirit 1 simply because they got fed up of all this spirit stuff happening around them and not having any way of understanding what was going on. They read a few books during downtime and started to study ways to measure spiritual energy, and from then on, they could at least keep up with everyone else once spirit stuff started to go down. It wasn\u2019t really their focus or interest, but it helped, at least for targeting spirits with magic stuff. (My ST probably should have left it to spirit 2 strictly speaking, but they allowed it)<br /> <br /> This mage had no interest in spirits otherwise, nor any real wish to ever traverse the umbra, not after the first time the crosses the gauntlet and their avatar was shredded, but with all the otherworldly stuff that was jumping out at them throughout the story, knowing at least a little Spirit was just becoming a necessity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair enough. Just having a functional understanding to *avoid* spirits and spirit-related problems is neat once you have enough magical power under your belt. My point is a general one however; I feel like it's the Sphere which benefits the most from skills lying outside of it, and wider Backgrounds and understanding.<br /> <br /> Take Forces. Sure, some Intelligence, Perception, Stamina... they're useful. An ability to focus it through, like Hyper-tech or yoga or brawl or computer.<br /> <br /> Then take Spirit. It's linked to many merits and backgrounds. It's linked to the Social attributes, Enigmas, Willpower, Occult lore, Expression, Etiquette, and it *can* be linked to all sorts of other things in a non-optional way. You can simply design a mage with Brawl, and then say &quot;oh yeah and fighting is their focus for X&quot;. With some Spirits, it isn't at all optional. If you're dealing with Squirrel, you'd better have the Abilities which Squirrel respects and the traits that it finds endearing. And a mage can specialize of course; focus on certain types of spirit, but sometimes you need to deal with spirits who have odd requests. To be genuinely powerful in a Spiritual sense, whilst still having some flexibility, you need to have a lot of traits backing you up. And those traits are useful outside of dealing with Spirits, of course, but I'd say it's the Sphere which comes with the longest list of important traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T16:09:32-07:00","id":1214817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214781#post1214781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fair enough. Just having a functional understanding to *avoid* spirits and spirit-related problems is neat once you have enough magical power under your belt. My point is a general one however; I feel like it's the Sphere which benefits the most from skills lying outside of it, and wider Backgrounds and understanding.<br /> <br /> Take Forces. Sure, some Intelligence, Perception, Stamina... they're useful. An ability to focus it through, like Hyper-tech or yoga or brawl or computer.<br /> <br /> Then take Spirit. It's linked to many merits and backgrounds. It's linked to the Social attributes, Enigmas, Willpower, Occult lore, Expression, Etiquette, and it *can* be linked to all sorts of other things in a non-optional way. You can simply design a mage with Brawl, and then say &quot;oh yeah and fighting is their focus for X&quot;. With some Spirits, it isn't at all optional. If you're dealing with Squirrel, you'd better have the Abilities which Squirrel respects and the traits that it finds endearing. And a mage can specialize of course; focus on certain types of spirit, but sometimes you need to deal with spirits who have odd requests. To be genuinely powerful in a Spiritual sense, whilst still having some flexibility, you need to have a lot of traits backing you up. And those traits are useful outside of dealing with Spirits, of course, but I'd say it's the Sphere which comes with the longest list of important traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a spirit for literally everything. Be it angels, ancestors, nymphs, old gods, new gods, aliens, and even memes. Any pantheon of spirits can be used for any character build imaginable, it\u2019s not as restricting as you\u2019re making it out to be.<br /> <br /> Besides, every sphere will change its behaviour depending on paradigm. Forces: is darkness a force distinct from light? Is coldness a force? Is there such thing as a vacuum and gravity and magnetisism? What about fire? If fire a reaction, a spiritual energy, or a pure element? Each answer subtly changes how the sphere reacts, for example if darkness is a force pattern distinct from light, you would need Forces 3 to Change light into dark and vise versa. However you could use Forces 2 to grab nearby darkness and wrap it around yourself, something which would not be possible if you believe darkness to just be the absence of light.<br /> <br /> Similarly, is life powered by the four humours, individual cells working to a whole, or do we just have a general spiritual life force.<br /> <br /> Does Time fly in a straight arrow, or is it curved around major events? Do the events of the past stay solid, or are they as open ended as the future?<br /> <br /> <br /> With Entropy, is the world determined or random? Do we control and change an otherwise immutable fate? Or are we just pushing the odds in our favour? Does randomness even exist or do we all have a path, or perhaps our actions as individuals are random and arbitrary, but the big stuff isn\u2019t. Changing history doesn\u2019t change the big events, only the names.<br /> <br /> Is the mind the same thing as the brain, or does it reside in a parallel world, in perfect synchronisation, yet utterly separate? Are memories events or merely repeating patterns? Can they be changed or merely influenced? Does identity lie in the mind or the soul?<br /> <br /> Is Quintessence the most fundamental particle of existence, and energy which permeates everything, a left behind relic of the greater beings, or the residual power of possibility? When you absorb it, do you become more powerful, or simply more physical? Can it be used for anything other than what it was intended for? Does the resonance it leaves on you depend on the source, the method of extraction, or the will of the deity who created it in the first place? When making a wonder, are you imbuing it with power, inventing a tool? Or are you for assistance from beings beyond your comprehension so they may imbue your tools with power? If the latter, then is it impossible to make something you know they won\u2019t like?<br /> <br /> No two mages spheres will work the same way. Even if they have exactly the same stats, the nuances in their paradigm will create different end results. A hermetic May cast a fireball which burns a blaze following an incantation of arcaic language. While a chorus member may ask for devine intervention, and before them their enemy now bursts into holy flames. An Etherite May instead zap them with a ray gun, while a Verbena may cut their hand and bleed out a wave of flame towards them.<br /> <br /> The Etherite would have to aim their shot, while the Hermetic may instead just need to focus on their linguistics. The choristers magic may only work if their deity wills it to, while the Verbena may need to take a single health level of damage to pull of the effect.<br /> <br /> Differences are built into each aspect of the character and every sphere, Spirit is not the exception, but the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 05-03-2018, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T16:35:11-07:00","id":1214827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214817#post1214817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There\u2019s a spirit for literally everything. Be it angels, ancestors, nymphs, old gods, new gods, aliens, and even memes. Any pantheon of spirits can be used for any character build imaginable, it\u2019s not as restricting as you\u2019re making it out to be.<br /> <br /> Besides, every sphere will change its behaviour depending on paradigm. Forces: is darkness a force distinct from light? Is coldness a force? Is there such thing as a vacuum and gravity and magnetisism? What about fire? If fire a reaction, a spiritual energy, or a pure element? Each answer subtly changes how the sphere reacts, for example if darkness is a force pattern distinct from light, you would need Forces 3 to Change light into dark and vise versa. However you could use Forces 2 to grab nearby darkness and wrap it around yourself, something which would not be possible if you believe darkness to just be the absence of light.<br /> <br /> [Snip]<br /> <br /> Differences are built into each aspect of the character and every sphere, Spirit is not the exception, but the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. But that doesn't contradict anything I said.<br /> <br /> Every Sphere varies from tradition to tradition, from convention to convention, and from mage to mage. But the vast majority of applications of Spirit, the core of the Sphere if you will (social interaction with Spirits) involves a huge catalogue of different important traits. Sure, you *can* summon up a potent alien/incarna/angel, but if your Charisma, Manipulation, Willpower, Wits, Perception, Intelligence, Enigmas, Occult, Etiquette etc. etc. etc. aren't up to the mark then you might get a negative result. If only you'd known that Lion would respond terribly to that sort of greeting. If only you'd known that this precise spirit has developed a (justified) hatred of your Tradition after &quot;the incident&quot;. If only you'd known that this spirit would be offended if you didn't attach a certain title. If only you'd known that a blood offering would offend the &quot;thing&quot; you summoned. The Spirit Sphere opens up a complicated world; in fact, that's an understatement, a complex set of worlds, to the Mage. You're diving into a nest of pernicious demi-gods who (rightly?) take a dim view to interfering mortals in many cases.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason Void Engineers suck at dealing with extradimensional creatures is that they don't know to make offerings, and would actively reject such an idea. It seems so... mystical. What you're dealing with is a scientific phenomena, and paying a sort of homage affords them a degree of humanity which is unscientific, and falls in line with the works of reality deviants. There's a reason Dimensional Science is so focused on travel, and fighting spirits. The fact that they enter the game without the centuries of cross-tradition information available to members of the Traditions is a huge disadvantage. And in exchange, they are WAY better at other things, like weakening the Gauntlet and moving through other dimensions. But their inefficacy in dealing with aliens (although there are exceptions) is proof of my point.<br /> <br /> And when contrasted with Forces... you make stuff stop being alive, and you generally destroy things. Sure, your Focus can be as complicated as anything (mind-bending contortions, cries in dead languages, hypertech contraptions which weigh half a tonne) but at the end of the day the most complicated conjunctional traits needed here will be aiming, hitting, and whatever Ability you're using as a Focus.<br /> <br /> Now you could argue that Mind has similar requirements. Mind will be much more coincidental and powerful when combined with charisma, manipulation, certain merits, high Willpower... but interpersonal interaction is an inescapable aspect of a Mage character. It's part of TTRPG and human existence. Spirits are generally alien and have inhuman (although this doesn't necessarily mean inhumane) principles and interests.<br /> <br /> So it's not that Spirit is conceptually restricting or limiting, it's that Spirit requires quite a lot of conceptual and mechanical *investment* to be given justice. And that could look like a million different things. Just working off of &quot;interferes with powers that shouldn't be interfered with&quot; you can come up with a Hermetic (demons, infernal spirits), a Dreamspeaker (banes, corrupted spirits), a Void Engineer (performs unauthorized procedures with mysterious aliens which promise incredible power to them) and a Virtual Adept (viral, corrupted and generally unpleasant technological/data spirits) quite easily. But regardless of how it's done, in my opinion, it should be quite a big part of who they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-03-2018, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T16:43:02-07:00","id":1214836,"title":"","content":"Or you could just use it to be a ghostbuster of sorts, have an awakened house and throw your enemies through portals to the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Just because you can summon spirits in theory doesn\u2019t mean you have to invest energy into it if it\u2019s of no interest to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T17:07:58-07:00","id":1214841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1213515-transmuting-an-attack-into-quintessence?p=1214836#post1214836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just use it to be a ghostbuster of sorts, have an awakened house and throw your enemies through portals to the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Just because you can summon spirits in theory doesn\u2019t mean you have to invest energy into it if it\u2019s of no interest to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you can just KOS all potentially problematic spirits, focus on the animistic side of material things and use portals to the umbra to solve problems (although you're relying on a thin gauntlet and 10+ successes to open a physical portal to the Umbra for other people, as opposed to just stepping through the gauntlet yourself (and naturally this is all vulgar), so this isn't really a good reason to take the Sphere; throwing people into the Umbra isn't a simple way of getting rid of them).<br /> <br /> If you take out social interaction with Spirits, you're removing most of the Sphere's potential. There are still a lot of effects on the table, and they're useful, sure, but unless you're a Void Engineer (in which case you have advantages to make up for the anti-social elements) you're wasting a lot of potential IMO, both mechanically and in terms of story. And honestly, handling violent spirits, gaining marginal (and largely non-mechanical) benefits from rousing objects, and stepping sideways... I mean they're all cool enough. They're handy. But so much is missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T17:34:48-07:00","id":1214848,"title":"","content":"First point, you can use Spirit 2 to thin out the gauntlet. It\u2019s really not that big a deal.<br /> <br /> Second point, you can say the same thing about wonder crafting with Prime, Time travel with Time, total mind control with Mind, or controlling the weather with Forces.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s great that you think the spiritual interactions side of Spirit is such a key part of the sphere, but it\u2019s not the only part there is, and to imply that if you have no interest in it you\u2019re in some way \u201cdoing it wrong\u201d is somewhat disappointing.<br /> <br /> You can be interested in Entropy without exploiting the dice roll affecting side of it, you can play with corresspondence for its increased range and ignore the teleportation side of it, and you can have spirit without needing to be all chummy chummy with the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Just like you don\u2019t need chemistry knowledge to be an Etherite, you don\u2019t have to have spirit buddies to want self aware pens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 05-03-2018, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T23:00:52-07:00","id":1214927,"title":"","content":"Two void engineers are discussing about never doing offering again:<br /> <br /> - And you give it three fiddy ? No wonders it asks for more.<br /> - Yeah, stupid lochness monster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}